Dockerfile integration for all dgxarley sgl-kernel patches.

Structural changes to container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly:

1. Six new ARGs near the top of the builder stage:
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_ARCH_PRUNE       default 1 — arch list prune
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_DISABLE_FA3      default 1 — FA3 disable
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SKIP_SM90_TARGET default 1 — sm90 target skip
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SKIP_FLASHMLA    default 1 — flashmla_ops target skip
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121            default 1 — CORE sm121 JIT-header fix
     APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121_DEBUG      default 0 — sm121 gemm_op.run
                                                   post-launch error check
   The first four are every-build optimizations and default to ON. The
   fifth gates the core SM121 shared-memory fix (see point 5). The
   sixth is a diagnostic for CUTLASS sm120 GEMM template iteration work
   and stays OFF by default.

2. Add `patch` to the builder apt install list (the base image
   scitrera/dgx-spark-pytorch-dev does not ship the `patch` binary), and
   wrap that whole builder apt step in the connectivity retry loop of
   point 7.

3. MOVE the sglang Python package install (`uv pip install ./python`)
   from its original early position to the end of the builder stage,
   right before stages/directory_split2.sh runs.

4. EARLY patch application for the sgl-kernel CMakeLists edits. Four
   patches (arch-prune, disable-fa3, skip-sm90-target, skip-flashmla)
   MUST be applied BEFORE the `uv build --wheel` of sgl-kernel because
   they edit sgl-kernel/CMakeLists.txt which is read at CMake configure
   time. Each independently gated by a build-arg.

5. LATE patch application for sgl-kernel-sm121.patch + the optional
   sgl-kernel-sm121-debug.patch (post-launch error diagnostic). Both
   target the JIT-compiled nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh header. Placing
   these late keeps iteration fast — changing either patch only
   invalidates the final layers, not the expensive sgl-kernel wheel
   build.

   Both are wrapped in APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121 (default 1, so every
   pre-v0.5.16 recipe behaves exactly as before). Set the recipe knob
   APPLY_SGL_KERNEL_SM121=0 on SGLang >= v0.5.16: PR #30448 ("Refactor
   FP4 quantization and remove deprecated JIT kernels", 2026-07-14)
   DELETED python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/moe/nvfp4_blockwise_moe.cuh
   together with cutlass_moe_fp4(), so the dry-run inside this RUN would
   abort the build. On those refs NVFP4 MoE dispatches to
   FlashInfer-CUTLASS on SM100/SM120/SM121, which is what our model
   profiles already select (moe_runner_backend: flashinfer_cutlass).
   The two COPY steps stay unconditional so the build context (and
   therefore the layer cache key) does not depend on the toggle.

6. Add runtime debug/init tooling to the RUNTIME stage apt list (the
   one that lands in the final serving image, NOT the builder stage):
   tini, iproute2, iputils-ping, net-tools, ethtool. These give the
   served SGLang pods an init binary plus in-pod network diagnostics
   (ip/ping/ifconfig/ethtool) — useful for QSFP/RoCE/VF debugging. curl
   is already present in the runtime list, so it is not re-added. The
   runtime apt step is likewise wrapped in the retry loop of point 7.

7. Wrap BOTH apt steps (builder + runtime) in a bounded connectivity
   retry loop, so a transient loss of connectivity to the Ubuntu package
   mirrors does not fail the whole (long, expensive arm64) image build.
   Mirrors the runtime launch script's idiom, adapted for a build:
     - `Acquire::ForceIPv4 "true"` drop-in (the cluster forces IPv4 for
       apt anyway — see commit "Force IPv4-only DNS and apt traffic").
     - swap the lossy default arm64 mirror ports.ubuntu.com/ubuntu-ports
       -> ftp.fau.de/ubuntu-ports (best-effort `sed`, `|| true`).
     - `apt_ok=false; for i in $(seq 1 10); do apt-get update -qq; if
       apt-get install …; then apt_ok=true; break; fi; sleep 5; done`.
   Key difference vs the runtime script (which warns-and-continues): a
   BUILD must not ship a half-installed image, so after 10 failed
   attempts the loop ABORTS the build with `exit 1` and a clear
   "no connectivity to Ubuntu package servers" diagnostic. The
   non-network tail of each RUN (builder `ln -s`; both `rm -rf
   /var/lib/apt/lists/*` + runtime `pip install uv`) stays OUTSIDE the
   loop. No `#` comments live inside these RUNs — shell-form joins every
   continued line into one, where a `#` would comment out the remainder.

8. Set ENV DGXARLEY_RUNTIME_LIBS_BAKED=1 in the RUNTIME stage (right after the
   runtime apt/pip step). The runtime launch script
   (roles/k8s_dgx/files/sglang_launch.sh) reads it to SKIP its own apt bootstrap
   entirely — our image bakes the runtime deps in, so a served pod never touches
   the (lossy, US-hosted) Ubuntu mirror at start. Stock upstream images (no marker)
   still install via that script's FAU-mirror + retry loop.

9. Build-time smoke test at the END of the RUNTIME stage:
     RUN python3 -c "import cutlass.cute; import sglang.srt.models.deepseek_v2, glm4_moe"
   FAILS the build (instead of shipping a broken image) if the pinned cutlass-dsl
   version drops cutlass.cute. Its absence silently unregisters every
   DeepSeek-V2-derived model class (DeepSeek-V2/V3/V4, GLM-5/glm_moe_dsa) and
   forces the slow/broken Transformers backend — caught at BUILD, not at deploy.

Idempotency: Every patch application is preceded by a dry-run so
upstream drift fails immediately with a clear diagnostic instead of
producing a half-patched image. Post-apply `grep -q '<marker>'` calls
act as positive verification that the patch text actually landed in
the target file.

Apply to: container-build/Dockerfile.sglang-nightly in the local
clone of scitrera/cuda-containers. The sm121 branch in that clone
carries this patch; see scripts/build_sm121_image.sh.

10. ARG SGL_KERNEL_DIR (default "sgl-kernel") — where the sgl-kernel source
   tree lives inside the sglang checkout. SGLang RFC #29630 finished in
   v0.5.17 and MOVED the whole tree from sgl-kernel/ at the repo root to
   python/sglang/kernels/aot/ (same "sglang-kernel" package name and
   version, same CMakeLists.txt/Makefile, just relocated). Three places
   consume it: the SGLANG_VERSION sed on the kernel pyproject, the four
   post-apply `grep -q '<marker>' <dir>/CMakeLists.txt` verifications, and
   the `cd <dir>` of the wheel build. The default reproduces the previous
   hardcoded paths byte-for-byte, so every pre-v0.5.17 recipe is unaffected;
   the v0.5.17 recipe sets SGL_KERNEL_DIR=python/sglang/kernels/aot and
   pairs it with the *-v0.5.17 CMakeLists patch variants (whose diff headers
   carry the new path). Without it the build dies at `cd sgl-kernel`.

